525.I8.G5513 1984"],"key":"/books/OL3184564M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL1471A","name":"al-Ghazzālī"}],"ocaid":"marriagesexualit0000ghaz","publish_places":["Salt Lake City, Utah"],"contributions":["Farah, Madelain."],"pagination":"xii, 185 p. ;","source_records":["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part16.dat:120080368:1040","ia:marriagesexualit0000ghaz","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part14.utf8:189464922:1059","bwb:9780874802313","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-001.mrc:315281979:1534","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.00.20150123.full.mrc:192256213:1086","idb:9780874802313","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_013.bib.mrc:205427011:3727"],"title":"Marriage and sexuality in Islam","dewey_decimal_class":["297/.19783581"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Bibliography: p. [169]-177.\nTranslation of the twelfth book of the author's Iḥyāʼ ʻulūm al-dīn.\nOriginally presented as the translator's thesis (doctoral--University of Utah)\nIncludes index."},"identifiers":{"goodreads":["756096"],"librarything":["7991895"]},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"},{"key":"/languages/ara"}],"lccn":["83027365"],"subjects":["Marriage -- Religious aspects -- Islam -- Early works to 1800"],"publish_date":"1984","publish_country":"utu","by_statement":"by Madelain Farah.","work_title":["Iḥyāʼ ʻulūm al-dīn. Book 12."],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL304813W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"oclc_numbers":["10301114"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Islam considers marriage as the most intimate communion between man and woman. The mystery of sex finds it fulfilment when intimate spiritual harmony is combined with the physical link. Marriage and family laws are, therefore, an important part of Islamic law for the fulfilment of its ultimate objective of building a harmonious and peaceful human society. In his inimitable style, Imam al-Ghazali, may Allah be pleased with him, discusses this subject in this small book, and shows how Islam, despite differences in rules and marriage, sets out inviolable principles so that marriage is not distorted by godless understandings now threatening to dehumanise many a society of both the East and West. The Islamic code of marriage and family is second to none in importance in helping to lead a life of goodness and purity."},"latest_revision":13,"revision":13,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-08-12T14:36:24.047353"}}},"ISBN:9783487059563":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9783487059563","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL3897346M/Islamische_Ethik_nach_den_Originalquellen_übersetzt_und_erläutert","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL3897346M/Islamische_Ethik_nach_den_Originalquellen_übersetzt_und_erläutert","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4337448-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["G. Olms"],"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Heft 1. Über Intention, reine Absicht und Wahrhaftigkeit.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Heft 2. Von der Ehe.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Heft 3. Erlaubtes und verbotenes Gut.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Heft 4. Vom Gottvertrauen.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"isbn_10":["3487059568"],"covers":[4337448],"lc_classifications":["BJ1291 .G415215"],"key":"/books/OL3897346M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL1471A","name":"al-Ghazzālī"}],"publish_places":["Hildesheim","New York"],"contributions":["Bauer, Hans, 1878-1937."],"pagination":"4 v. in 1 ;","source_records":["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part13.dat:93460507:1216","marc:marc_university_of_toronto/uoft.marc:5367996963:1260","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part13.utf8:192319538:1265","bwb:9783487059563","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.01.20150123.full.mrc:25495519:1185"]